[
    {
        "content": "<p>For Rényi/Shannon entropy on a finite alphabet, would Mathlib want <code>stdSimplex ℝ (Fin n) ≃ PMF (Fin n)</code> somewhere? Convexity arguments want <code>stdSimplex</code>, while push-forwards/products want <code>PMF</code>. Preferred home: <code>StdSimplex</code>, <code>ProbabilityMassFunction</code>, or a small bridge file?</p>",
        "id": 591251861,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1777334079
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think we should have the more general</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PMF</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">equivStdSimplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PMF</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">≃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stdSimplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 591252469,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1777334476
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"310045\">@Eric Wieser</span> thank you!</p>",
        "id": 591253121,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1777334654
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In fact, <code>Finite</code> is better than <code>Fintype</code> here, edited above</p>",
        "id": 591253382,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1777334712
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Got it. I’ll use the generic <code>[Finite ι]</code> version and keep the <code>Fin n</code> specialization downstream</p>",
        "id": 591254281,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1777334863
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I highly doubt you need the specialization at all</p>",
        "id": 591259032,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1777336445
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That makes more sense. No need for the specialized coordinate representation.</p>",
        "id": 591261456,
        "sender_full_name": "Nelson Spence",
        "timestamp": 1777338037
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/generic.20shannon.20entropy.20formalization.20mathlib4/with/584361371\">https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/generic.20shannon.20entropy.20formalization.20mathlib4/with/584361371</a></p>",
        "id": 591281365,
